WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:52.000
(Casting)

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.740
"Like the truth is Aphro went
to the org and he said it's either me or

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:58.240
him."

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.860
"I mean Peter can be a dick and talk

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.920
bad about everyone that he wants to talk
bad about but ultimately I don't care."

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.880
"I feel like people have a really like
skewed perception of me and Aphro."

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.120
"I mean that's cool. If he wants to hate me that's fine."

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.920
"To me I feel like he gave up on me

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.380
as a friend and as a teammate."

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.680
"Organization thought it would be the

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:32.460
best decision moving forward only
because Peter brings people down more

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.440
often than not."

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.280
"I think we can all agree
that I'm way better off on TSM and I

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.490
think TSM wins, I win and CLG ultimately wins because if

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:46.540
they really hate me so bad then now they
don't have to deal with me."

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.160
Aphromoo wanted something different.
Doublelift's attitude was bringing down

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:57.670
the team and Aphro wanted to take a
leadership role for everyone. He wasn't

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:04.680
just the team's leader, he was their big
brother. He was Mr. CLG. This is his story

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:14.180
Zaqueri “Aphromoo” Black was born on September 8, 1992 in Whittier, California,

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:19.390
and took to video games at a young age.
Aphromoo played Diablo with his dad

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.170
and eventually moved to playing
competitive World of Warcraft even,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.610
playing on LAN at BlizzCon. But Aphromoo eventually grew tired of PvP WoW

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.690
and turned to League of Legends.
Aphromoo started out as a streamer,

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:37.020
and gained  popularity thanks to his solid AD carry play and loud personality.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.640
But Aphromoo wasn’t just a popular streamer, he played at a high level, and

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.280
pros quickly took notice. Unfortunately, none of them seemed to stick

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.880
and Aphromoo joined seven teams between 2011 and 2012.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:07.280
In late 2012, Aphromoo switched from AD carry to Support, and though he was playing a less

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:11.980
active role, he was still just as good, and just as bombastic.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.360
Aphromoo first joined CLG in

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:55.400
December 2012 as their starting support, sharing the bot lane with a man

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.500
considered the best AD Carry in North America, Doublelift.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:24.000
(Casting)

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.880
CLG placed fourth that season, but fell to last place in the playoffs, forcing

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.160
them to win their spot in the LCS back through the promotion tournament.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.580
"Now for CLG the stakes couldn't be higher.
On the line for Hotshot and crew is not

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:42.500
just a trip to the LCS but the very
existence of the team."

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:48.160
Despite Aphromoo’s talents, the team didn’t work, and he was the first to leave the team after they requalified.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.700
Aphromoo says that he stepped down, that he couldn’t handle the

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:56.710
pressure that came with being relied on by his entire team. The pressure of

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:00.360
playing with someone as demanding as Doublelift.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:10.000
CLG replaced Aphromoo with founding member Chauster in May. Aphro returned to

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:15.120
streaming and did that full-time until October, when he tried out for Team Curse

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.440
and made the team before getting a call from CLG’s mid laner Link.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:24.940
"I talked to Link and I saw Doublelift in Solo Q
and we played bottom lane again. I played

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:31.120
support and I guess he remembered me
after that. 'Oh yeah this guy still plays the game I guess so.'"

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:36.880
Aphromoo was back on CLG, and back with Doublelift. The best AD carry in North

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:41.360
America was back with one of the league’s brightest young support players.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.280
It seemed like the perfect match. But the pressure was still on.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.360
"Aphromoo was already on the team before and they
brought him back so that he could play

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:52.699
with Doublelift once again, exciting a
lot of the fans."

00:06:52.699 --> 00:06:56.750
Doublelift and Aphromoo quickly became one of the stronger bot lanes in NA, and

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:01.550
one of the most popular as well. As the years went on, they only got better and

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:05.720
their fandom grew even more.  The pair played up their friendship for the

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:09.220
camera, leaning on their personalities to create one of the most iconic

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.960
partnerships in League of Legends: Rush Hour.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.900
"Why did you guys seem like you

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:21.530
wanted to throw that game so badly." "Well
Doublelift didn't please me last night so

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:26.930
I was pretty mad and usually I take out
my rage in bottom lane and we saw that

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:27.430
today.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.200
But while Support is a selfless role, playing support for Doublelift is

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.580
an even more selfless act.
Doublelift is a hyper carry, which means

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:43.039
Aphromoo’s entire job was to set things up for his AD carry to succeed. No

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.140
roaming, no playmaking, no glory.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:08:10.000
(Casting)

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:14.680
Both players had big personalities, but as they played together more, Aphromoo’s

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:18.470
started to mellow out. Where Doublelift got louder, Aphromoo

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.850
started taking a more quiet leadership role on the team, taking on shotcalling

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.180
duties and even getting more pensive in interviews.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:30.400
"What are you guys looking at as kind of your real opponents right now and who's gonna give you some trouble

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:38.779
final question." "Honestly I don't really
talk down most of the teams in league

00:08:38.779 --> 00:08:41.270
they're really good and really fun to
play against." "Good policy." "Especially

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:46.480
Enemy as you've seen right here.
TSM, Team Liquid, Dignitas, Enemy and

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:49.460
that's all I can think of right now
they're all looking really good and

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.279
they're really fun to play against and
that's all that really matters and we

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.180
just have to execute our plan as well as
we can."

00:08:55.180 --> 00:09:02.740
The shotcalling position was taking its toll on Aphromoo. Every season, CLG’s team looked strong, but they never

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:06.200
quite managed to put together a win in the playoffs.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:20.000
(Casting)

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.320
The pressure on Aphromoo was

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:26.150
mounting as his team looked to him to lead them to victory. He was still the

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:29.839
same fun-loving guy he was on stream all those years ago,

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:34.620
but on stage, he was a professional. And he wanted to win.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.760
In Summer 2015, Aphromoo finally got his wish.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.840
CLG looked better than ever. They placed second in the regular season, and went

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:52.000
undefeated in the playoffs, where they beat Team SoloMid 3-0 in the Grand Finals.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:16.460
(Casting)

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:20.760
You’d expect Aphromoo to be ecstatic. You’d expect him to be happy.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.950
But Aphromoo was just relieved. "I was
just like whatever. I think I relish in

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:30.600
the fact that I know all my teammates
are happy that we won. More so than,

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.050
you know me being happy that we won. You
know I just like seeing them you know

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:38.940
excited and I'm happy that you know all
the work that we put in you know we got

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:39.620
to where we went."

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:48.499
CLG went on to Worlds after their win at MSG, but failed to make it out of their group. And things were only going

00:10:48.499 --> 00:10:54.619
get tougher for Aphromoo. "Hey my name is
Doublelift and starting today I'll be a

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.969
part of TSM." Doublelift’s departure wasn’t necessarily his own decision.

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:04.399
Aphromoo was the one who called for a shakeup in CLG. "Like the truth is Aphro

00:11:04.399 --> 00:11:09.139
went to the org and he said it's either
me or him." "Great branding, one of the most

00:11:09.139 --> 00:11:13.549
popular players in the league, has a
great franchise, you know, but the trade

00:11:13.549 --> 00:11:17.449
off just wasn't that good." "I'm not ever
gonna deny that I made a lot of mistakes

00:11:17.449 --> 00:11:20.809
but the thing is that I tried really
hard to fix them and I was getting

00:11:20.809 --> 00:11:25.099
better and improving and there's like
interviews and a lot of proof where my

00:11:25.099 --> 00:11:28.819
teammates and coach had said that I made
a lot of progress and I wasn't just

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:30.480
trying to improve I was improving."

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.840
"We tried to for three years. I was on the team

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.699
for three years obviously. And you know
get better little by little attitude you

00:11:37.699 --> 00:11:43.879
know but team chemistry-wise and the
impact he had on the team in general

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:49.519
just atmosphere-wise, being in a personal
relationship with people is just it just

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.940
brings people down you know every season."

00:11:55.320 --> 00:12:00.240
Aphromoo was given control of a new CLG team for the upcoming spring season, and

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:04.900
was preparing to lane with a fresh faced AD carry Stixxay.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:32.040
Stixxay was young and new to the pro scene. He had played in challenger, but Aphromoo was the one who

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.420
shepherded him on to the big stage.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.400
"So when Stixxay came to play he was very calm

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:42.100
mellow and when I play with him in lane
he would kill somebody who I didn't

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.680
think we would kill I was like what the
hell dude."

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:51.480
I didn't know you could get that guy, that was insane."
Aphromoo saw Stixxay as a younger

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:55.420
brother, but he also had plenty to learn from him. Breaking free of Doublelift’s

00:12:55.420 --> 00:13:00.520
play and attitude let Aphromoo come into his own as a playmaker and shotcaller

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:47.000
(Casting)

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.920
CLG’s roster was unproven but with
Aphromoo at the helm

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:58.850
CLG quickly became one of the best teams
in the league that season. He was proving

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.170
that it wasn’t just Doublelift carrying CLG, he was an important part of the team’s

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.360
success as well.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:39.000
(Casting)

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:44.060
Aphromoo led CLG to another NA LCS championship, this time

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.940
with a 3-2 win over TSM in the spring 2016 grand finals.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:15:27.000
(Casting)

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.500
And CLG wasn't done. The

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:34.070
team went to the Mid-Season Invitational after playoffs, where they were pegged as

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.960
as one of the weaker teams at the event.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.120
"So the thing about CLG is I actually don't

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:41.420
think they're a bad team, I just have
questions about their team on the

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:45.139
international stage and I think there's
three of them. Can Xmithie step up the way he

00:15:45.139 --> 00:15:48.440
did in the finals. He diversified his
champion pools very well, not only

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:52.490
supportive but also very aggressive but
Stixxay, Huhi, I think that there are

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:56.779
huge questions about Huhi, he doesn't
get banned out very much what else can

00:15:56.779 --> 00:15:59.930
he play. And Stixxay's champion pool
to me, I don't know whether it's good or

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:05.029
bad but it's bizarre man." But Aphromoo led CLG to second place, taking games off

00:16:05.029 --> 00:16:11.960
of Royal Never Give Up, the Flash Wolves, G2 Esports and SK Telecom T1 in the process.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:17:15.600
(Casting)

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:47.000
(Casting)

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:48.940
Aphromoo wasn’t sad about the

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:52.990
loss. In fact, he said it was an opportunity to learn and understand

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:56.980
where he had to lead his team to next. "We
definitely learned a lot and being able

00:17:56.980 --> 00:18:00.760
to play against all the teams and making
it all the way to finals we have a lot

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:06.520
of knowledge that we can use for our
play and going into NA LCS I think that

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.820
NA as a region will probably do a lot
better at Worlds this time around

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:15.760
definitely really confident in saying
that." Aphromoo proved once again that, no

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:20.020
matter what his team looks like, no matter who his opponents are, he was the

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:24.980
stabilizing, leading presence teams need to make championship runs.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:32.120
For his part, Aphromoo continued to get more and more measured in his public

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:36.810
appearances. He could still crack a joke, but being the guy his teammates relied

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:41.670
appearances. Being the most respected leader in the NA LCS made Aphromoo more pensive,

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:45.000
more thoughtful. "I don't think too much
has changed like with his personality

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.390
throughout the two or three years I've
known him. He's been pretty much the same

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:52.350
person but now he's a lot more like
commanding or like demanding of like

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:56.730
what he really wants and as far as like
gameplay or anything like that goes

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:02.370
before he was less of a natural leader
and now he's like a very like powerful

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:07.800
person within the team." As the seasons passed, Aphromoo stuck with CLG. Others came

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:13.770
and went, but Aphromoo was always there. He was Mister CLG, the team leader, the

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:18.240
company man, always there as the star support and leader the team looked to

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:23.640
when things looked rough. But CLG wasn't
winning championships anymore Aphromoo

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:27.870
needed a shake-up
and when NA LCS franchising hit, new

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:31.320
teams were knocking at his door. "I never
you know looked at my other options

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:37.350
besides CLG since I thought that that
would be my home forever but here we are."

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:42.060
100 Thieves wanted a star support. They wanted a great leader who could

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:46.380
show a brand new organization the way. They wanted experience and a stabilizing

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:50.850
presence. They wanted Aphromoo. "We are so
incredibly proud and excited to welcome

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:55.920
Aphromoo as the support player for the
100 Thieves' roster moving into the 2018

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.840
LCS. We got Aphromoo!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:07.760
While they’re still a young team, 100 Thieves have done well so far. They’ve

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:10.980
beaten CLG, with Aphromoo leading them to victory.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:32.000
(Casting)

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:36.140
But most importantly, Aphromoo has become the kind of veteran that he

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:40.780
looked up to all those years ago. "Stixxay,
who you essentially helped train and

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:45.730
grow, was playing against him a proud dad
moment or was it a I'm gonna put this

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:51.790
kid in his place." "Trevor is a good kid. He
actually has really good mechanics it

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:55.120
was really hard to land a skill-shot on
him. Usually I have that on my team from

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:59.050
playing on CLG right but uh CLG's
gonna do well. They are a new team coming

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:02.680
together from the jungle and support
roles as well but they just need a

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:05.800
little bit of time they'll be fine." He has one of the longest careers in North

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.940
American League of Legends, and has gone from a goofy streamer to one of the most

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:14.500
respected shot callers in the league. We don’t know how long Aphromoo will keep

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:20.400
playing, but he’ll always have a place as one of the North American League of Legends most important figures.

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:28.720
He might not have dozens of trophies, but he has something just as important: the respect that comes with being the ultimate support.

